# Force LF on checkout for files Docker executes. A Windows clone with the
# default core.autocrlf=true otherwise produces CRLF shell scripts, which
# build fine but fail at container start with:
#   exec /docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# Scoped deliberately: no blanket "* text=auto". Existing files in this repo
# are already LF, so these rules change checkout behavior only -- they do not
# rewrite history or touch the RTF/XML spec captures that legitimately hold CRLF.

*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*  text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
